<!-- cell: markdown id="1bb474c2-e1e6-4730-a599-46d86404afb5" -->

# How the war begun

## High-level plot

1. Earth finds an artifact on Mars and begin excavating.

2. The artifact is actually a living organism and the excavation is damaging it. It sends a signal to its race, who come to protect it.

3. Earth sees the ships coming out of hyper-space, and thinks it's an attack. 

4. War begins.

## Low-level plot

The space agency on Earth spots an irregular shape under Mars's surface in a probe's scans, and broadcasts the finding worldwide.

Excavation team is sent, robots are lowered down and begin excavating

Excavation uncovers the object made out of rare materials, resembling a stone sculpture. 

Samples are sent to orbit, to a laboratory ship. Scientists begin studying the object.

The object is an organism embedded in the rock. It was monitoring the probe's movement and its scan, and the arrival of the excavation team.

The excavation begins, and the organism grows concern. But it's not until the excavators pierce its exoskeleton, hurting it, that is sends a distress call.

The communication is FTL, he is asked what is the nautre of emergency. The organism says he was discovered and attacked. He is told to stay put and that help is on the way.

Alien ships emerge on a far orbit around Mars. Earth ships spot them immediately. 

Earth sends orders to protect the discovery. The mission consists of the lab ship and one weakly armed escort. 

Ships are approaching, they are completely foreign and no one on the earth ships knows how to even interpret if they are powering up weapons or not. hails are sent, but to no effect.

Scientists on the lab ship are scrambling in attempt to understand anything about the alien ships. They suspect they are here for the artifact, and they are trying to correlate what they found with the sensor readings. The mineral scans agree, the origin seems the same, but that doesn't say anything about communication.

All the while the excavation efforts are not stoping, the scientists wanting to find out more about the fleet that approaches by studying the object buried on Mars.

The object communicates with the fleet that he is in need of dire assistance.

The fleet observes the efforts and identifies the ships in orbit, classifying them as belionging to the same tribe as the entities attacking the object.

They fire on the ships in orbit, decimating them.

They automated excavators stop.

Earth notices the disapeparance of the ships, and assumes they have just been attacked in an act of war.

